IMPORT prelude

-- Supply Act 2025 (Singapore, No. 11 of 2025) -- commencement (s 1), the sums authorised to be issued from the Consolidated Fund
-- (s 2) and the Development Fund (s 3) for 1 April 2025 to 31 March 2026, and the Schedule of Heads of Expenditure.
--
-- Edition: as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/SA2025.txt. Every page of the deposit is marked "Informal Consolidation
-- -- version in force from 1/4/2025"; the retrieval record (SA2025.meta.json) says "Current version as at 01 Oct 2026". No
-- amendment is annotated in the text.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0222 in subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl: tier 3 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has
-- asked a sharper question yet. The honest answer, from the text, is: nothing directly. The Act authorises the issue of money and
-- appropriates it to Heads of Expenditure. It confers no right, imposes no duty and creates no offence. What it does fix -- two
-- ceilings, a period and a table of heads -- is encoded in full: the whole Act is three sections and a Schedule.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: the long title beyond its period; who may issue money and how (that is the Constitution and the Financial
-- Procedure Act, not read); the Supplementary Supply (FY 2025) Act 2026, which is deposited as a separate subject and not read;
-- anything below the level of a Head (the Act lists none).
--
-- THE SCHEDULE IS COLUMN-SHIFTED in the deposit's text layer: figures for different heads sit on the same line, and the totals of
-- one head appear beside the name of another. It was rebuilt by ORDER and ARITHMETIC: on each page the Consolidated Fund figures
-- were taken in the order printed and assigned to the heads in the order printed; each was paired with the one Development Fund
-- figure that, added to it, gives one of the printed totals (each such pairing is unique); and the column sums were checked
-- against the printed Total row and against ss 2(1) and 3(1). Where the deposit prints "..." or nothing in the Development Fund
-- column (heads D, G and Z) this encoding records 0 -- an inference from the printed total equalling the Consolidated Fund figure.
-- The PDF was not consulted. The Schedule runs B to Z with no Head A, H or Y; the text does not say why.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules conventions of the example rows. No pipeline, no
-- coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. NOT for public use. See NOTES.md.

§ `Supply Act 2025 -- nouns`

DECLARE Fund IS ONE OF
    `the Consolidated Fund`
    `the Development Fund`

DECLARE Head IS ONE OF
    `B Attorney-General's Chambers`
    `C Auditor-General's Office`
    `D Cabinet Office`
    `E Judicature`
    `F Parliament`
    `G Presidential Councils`
    `I Ministry of Social and Family Development`
    `J Ministry of Defence`
    `K Ministry of Education`
    `L Ministry of Sustainability and the Environment`
    `M Ministry of Finance`
    `N Ministry of Foreign Affairs`
    `O Ministry of Health`
    `P Ministry of Home Affairs`
    `Q Ministry of Digital Development and Information`
    `R Ministry of Law`
    `S Ministry of Manpower`
    `T Ministry of National Development`
    `U Prime Minister's Office`
    `V Ministry of Trade and Industry`
    `W Ministry of Transport`
    `X Ministry of Culture, Community and Youth`
    `Z Financial Transfers`

-- A calendar date is reduced to one comparable number, yyyymmdd. (A helper of this encoding, not of the Act.)
GIVEN y IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, d IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the date key` MEANS y * 10000 + m * 100 + d

§§ `1 -- commencement`

-- s 1: "This Act is the Supply Act 2025 and comes into operation on 1 April 2025."
GIVEN y IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, d IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Act is in operation on` IF
    `the date key` y m d >= 20250401

§§ `2 and 3 -- the sums authorised and the period`

-- s 2(1): "A sum of not more than $139,804,307,900 is authorised to be issued from the Consolidated Fund for the period starting
-- 1 April 2025 and ending 31 March 2026." (2): it "is appropriated for the Heads of Expenditure for the public service specified in
-- the Schedule".
-- s 3(1): "A sum of not more than $39,236,834,600 is authorised to be issued from the Development Fund" for the same period. (2): it
-- "is appropriated for development purposes under the Heads of Expenditure specified in the Schedule".
GIVEN fund IS A Fund
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the sum authorised from` MEANS
    CONSIDER fund
    WHEN `the Consolidated Fund` THEN 139804307900
    WHEN `the Development Fund` THEN 39236834600

GIVEN y IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, d IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the date falls in the supply period` IF
        `the date key` y m d >= 20250401
    AND `the date key` y m d <= 20260331

-- READING (an inference): "a sum of not more than" is a ceiling on everything issued from that Fund under the section for the
-- period, so an issue is within s 2(1) or s 3(1) only if it, added to what has already been issued under it, does not exceed the
-- sum. The Act says nothing about issues outside the period; this encoding treats them as not authorised BY THIS ACT.
GIVEN fund IS A Fund, `amount already issued` IS A NUMBER, `amount of this issue` IS A NUMBER,
      y IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, d IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the issue is within the authority of this Act` IF
        `the date falls in the supply period` y m d
    AND `amount already issued` + `amount of this issue` <= `the sum authorised from` fund

§§ `Schedule -- Heads of Expenditure`

-- The Schedule ("Sections 2(2) and 3(2)") has, for each Head, "Appropriation from Consolidated Fund $", "Appropriation from
-- Development Fund $" and "Total appropriations $". Rebuilt by order and arithmetic; see the header.
GIVEN head IS A Head
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Consolidated Fund appropriation for` MEANS
    CONSIDER head
    WHEN `B Attorney-General's Chambers` THEN 282435100
    WHEN `C Auditor-General's Office` THEN 46082000
    WHEN `D Cabinet Office` THEN 1100000
    WHEN `E Judicature` THEN 374860600
    WHEN `F Parliament` THEN 47784400
    WHEN `G Presidential Councils` THEN 1672800
    WHEN `I Ministry of Social and Family Development` THEN 5262330000
    WHEN `J Ministry of Defence` THEN 22099590500
    WHEN `K Ministry of Education` THEN 14647939200
    WHEN `L Ministry of Sustainability and the Environment` THEN 2658974300
    WHEN `M Ministry of Finance` THEN 1300315000
    WHEN `N Ministry of Foreign Affairs` THEN 576173800
    WHEN `O Ministry of Health` THEN 18795327500
    WHEN `P Ministry of Home Affairs` THEN 8027752000
    WHEN `Q Ministry of Digital Development and Information` THEN 2956698500
    WHEN `R Ministry of Law` THEN 356441800
    WHEN `S Ministry of Manpower` THEN 3584806700
    WHEN `T Ministry of National Development` THEN 8344980000
    WHEN `U Prime Minister's Office` THEN 1108629600
    WHEN `V Ministry of Trade and Industry` THEN 1638234500
    WHEN `W Ministry of Transport` THEN 2798018900
    WHEN `X Ministry of Culture, Community and Youth` THEN 2270827200
    WHEN `Z Financial Transfers` THEN 42623333500

-- "..." or blank in the deposit for D, G and Z: recorded as 0 (inference; see the header).
GIVEN head IS A Head
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Development Fund appropriation for` MEANS
    CONSIDER head
    WHEN `B Attorney-General's Chambers` THEN 5773100
    WHEN `C Auditor-General's Office` THEN 205000
    WHEN `D Cabinet Office` THEN 0
    WHEN `E Judicature` THEN 14914800
    WHEN `F Parliament` THEN 13746000
    WHEN `G Presidential Councils` THEN 0
    WHEN `I Ministry of Social and Family Development` THEN 209177400
    WHEN `J Ministry of Defence` THEN 2226482800
    WHEN `K Ministry of Education` THEN 852000000
    WHEN `L Ministry of Sustainability and the Environment` THEN 1477646700
    WHEN `M Ministry of Finance` THEN 127707700
    WHEN `N Ministry of Foreign Affairs` THEN 36600000
    WHEN `O Ministry of Health` THEN 2067888400
    WHEN `P Ministry of Home Affairs` THEN 1247341500
    WHEN `Q Ministry of Digital Development and Information` THEN 103188200
    WHEN `R Ministry of Law` THEN 138973500
    WHEN `S Ministry of Manpower` THEN 119216800
    WHEN `T Ministry of National Development` THEN 11140637200
    WHEN `U Prime Minister's Office` THEN 106620900
    WHEN `V Ministry of Trade and Industry` THEN 6309880900
    WHEN `W Ministry of Transport` THEN 12528311800
    WHEN `X Ministry of Culture, Community and Youth` THEN 510521900
    WHEN `Z Financial Transfers` THEN 0

GIVEN fund IS A Fund, head IS A Head
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the appropriation from` MEANS
    CONSIDER fund
    WHEN `the Consolidated Fund` THEN `the Consolidated Fund appropriation for` head
    WHEN `the Development Fund` THEN `the Development Fund appropriation for` head

GIVEN head IS A Head
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the total appropriation for` MEANS
    `the Consolidated Fund appropriation for` head + `the Development Fund appropriation for` head

GIVEN head IS A Head
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the head has a development appropriation` IF
    `the Development Fund appropriation for` head > 0

-- The sum of a Fund's column over every Head. ss 2(2) and 3(2) appropriate "the sum in subsection (1)" for the Heads in the
-- Schedule, so each column should add up to its section's sum; the cases assert that it does.
GIVEN fund IS A Fund
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Schedule column total for` MEANS
      `the appropriation from` fund `B Attorney-General's Chambers`
    + `the appropriation from` fund `C Auditor-General's Office`
    + `the appropriation from` fund `D Cabinet Office`
    + `the appropriation from` fund `E Judicature`
    + `the appropriation from` fund `F Parliament`
    + `the appropriation from` fund `G Presidential Councils`
    + `the appropriation from` fund `I Ministry of Social and Family Development`
    + `the appropriation from` fund `J Ministry of Defence`
    + `the appropriation from` fund `K Ministry of Education`
    + `the appropriation from` fund `L Ministry of Sustainability and the Environment`
    + `the appropriation from` fund `M Ministry of Finance`
    + `the appropriation from` fund `N Ministry of Foreign Affairs`
    + `the appropriation from` fund `O Ministry of Health`
    + `the appropriation from` fund `P Ministry of Home Affairs`
    + `the appropriation from` fund `Q Ministry of Digital Development and Information`
    + `the appropriation from` fund `R Ministry of Law`
    + `the appropriation from` fund `S Ministry of Manpower`
    + `the appropriation from` fund `T Ministry of National Development`
    + `the appropriation from` fund `U Prime Minister's Office`
    + `the appropriation from` fund `V Ministry of Trade and Industry`
    + `the appropriation from` fund `W Ministry of Transport`
    + `the appropriation from` fund `X Ministry of Culture, Community and Youth`
    + `the appropriation from` fund `Z Financial Transfers`

-- READING (an inference): the Act appropriates each Head's sum to that Head; a payment charged to a Head is within this Act's
-- appropriation only if, with what has already been charged to that Head from that Fund, it does not exceed the Head's figure.
-- (Virement between heads, if any, is not in this Act.)
GIVEN fund IS A Fund, head IS A Head, `already charged to the head` IS A NUMBER, `this charge` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the charge is within the head's appropriation` IF
    `already charged to the head` + `this charge` <= `the appropriation from` fund head
